1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,200
Imagine a hot day,

2
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:02,080
a hard run,

3
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:03,120
and instead of sweat,

4
00:00:03,120 --> 00:00:04,800
you start leaking Coca-Cola.

5
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,560
Sweat is almost pure water,

6
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:08,320
and it cools you by evaporating off

7
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:08,960
your skin.

8
00:00:08,960 --> 00:00:11,120
But cola is about one tenth sugar,

9
00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:12,720
and sugar doesn't evaporate.

10
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:14,000
So the water dries up,

11
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:15,520
and the sugar stays behind,

12
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:16,320
as a sticky,

13
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:17,280
brown glaze.

14
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:18,480
Your shirt stains,

15
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:20,160
your arms stick to your sides,

16
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:22,000
and the glaze can slow your cooling.

17
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Then every wasp and ant nearby smells

18
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:24,720
dessert.

19
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:26,880
Skin bacteria would feast on it too,

20
00:00:26,880 --> 00:00:28,560
so you'd probably smell worse.

21
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:30,320
And a hard workout would sweat out

22
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:32,400
nearly three cans of sugar an hour,

23
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:33,520
draining your energy.

24
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:35,280
So be glad your sweat is boring.

25
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:36,880
Salty water keeps you cool,

26
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:38,347
not candied.
